# Project media served locally while iterating on the design assets. Cloudinary bills on
# delivery, so pointing dev at it burns credits on every reload. These are ~14MB of
# iteration, not source: the master copies live in design-assets/, and every URL is
# swapped to Cloudinary in src/lib/assets.ts before production.
# NOTE: `npm run deploy` still publishes them, because Vite copies public/ into dist/ and
# gh-pages ships dist/. Ignoring them keeps the history lean, it does not un-deploy them.
public/img/

# The design masters: 2x exports, ~84MB, the source the files in public/img/ are downscaled
# from. Kept on disk and out of git, because they are an input to the build rather than part
# of the site, and a delivery at a time is more bytes than the whole repo.
# The trailing globs catch the next drop under whatever name it arrives with: three previous
# folders (desigassetnexports, newdesignassetexports, 9fixedassets) each sat in `git status`
# until they were consolidated into design-assets/.
design-assets/
*assetexports/
*fixedassets/
*designassets/
